{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550370527,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3898d76001DOIkXg8tP310PB","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d38949b0001RQnoKmnejxAALT","type":"tool","id":"call_0514af0a14cc478f8092ae7a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"openQuestions\":[],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/findings-registry.json"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/findings-registry.json","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/findings-registry.json"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"{\\\"openQuestions\\\":[],\\\"resolvedQuestions\\\":[],\\\"keyFindings\\\":[],\\\"ruledOutDirections\\\":[],\\\"metrics\\\":{\\\"iterationsCompleted\\\":0,\\\"openQuestions\\\":0,\\\"resolvedQuestions\\\":0,\\\"keyFindings\\\":0,\\\"convergenceScore\\\":0,\\\"coverageBySources\\\":{}}}\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/findings-registry.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550369654,"end":1794550370527}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550370532,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3895912001UFeNZJN4mo2syH","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d38949b0001RQnoKmnejxAALT","type":"tool","id":"call_b916a49a610b4ffbbbf7d27f","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach-3\ndescription: Segment three offer-reach lane: remaining plain tune rows after phase 012, intent-signal enrichment and re-embedding, and the degraded fallback path.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"offer reach segment three strategy\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\nversion: 1.0.0\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach-3\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the segment-three `offer-reach-3` fan-out lineage. Tracks what is left of the plain command-offer bottleneck after phases 011, 012 and 013, and the fallback path.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Read at every iteration before any research action.\n- Machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration; this file is not edited by the research agent.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nSEGMENT THREE offer-reach lane. Phases 011, 012 and 013 are built and committed. Find what still limits command surfacing, measured from the built state. Lane owns (a) which plain tune rows of `command-prompts.jsonl` still get no command after phase 012 and why, by row id, with the cause named per row (no command evidence, hub defers, below threshold, policy or cap, wrong top); and (b) intent-signal enrichment and re-embedding of the skill graph, declined in segment two at rank 15: which tune rows it would move, its risk to the floors, and the cost of keeping vectors in step with the metadata. Also carried, unassigned to a lane: (g) the degraded fallback path when the advisor daemon is unreachable, which runtimes hit it, how often, and the smallest change that makes the fallback carry the same command as the live answer. Floors: typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer eval [160,50,21,5].\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Which plain tune rows of command-prompts.jsonl still get no command after phase 012, and what is the cause per row id?\n- [ ] Would intent-signal enrichment and re-embedding of the skill graph move the remaining plain tune rows, and at what risk to the floors?\n- [ ] What does keeping the embedding vectors in step with the metadata cost, and how is drift detected?\n- [ ] Which runtimes hit the degraded fallback path in practice, and how often?\n- [ ] What is the smallest change that makes the fallback answer carry the same command as the live answer?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending anything already ranked, built, declined or eliminated in segment one (`research.md` plus the 009 `spec.md` dispositions) or segment two (`research-segment-2.md` sections 3 and 4). Reopen only with a new measurement that changes the disposition, naming the rank and the measurement.\n- Renaming an operator-facing command.\n- Starting any model CLI session, arena, daemon or Ollama server.\n- Reading holdout row prompt text or `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n- Editing any file outside this lineage directory.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at newInfoRatio 0.05 or below on two consecutive iterations, or 6 iterations, whichever comes first.\n- Both lane questions (a) and (b) answered with command output or file:line evidence, plus a named measurable recommendation each.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Approaches investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n\nIteration 1: enumerate the plain tune rows that still get no command after phase 012, from the committed capture's `attachedMetrics.plain` row state, and name a cause per row.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- `P/012-plain-offer-reach/implementation-summary.md`: plain tune 9 to 23 of 45; holdout plain 1 of 44; floors typed 24/44, false offers 0/35, eval [160,50,21,5]; `needsMode` label added; OpenCode plugin mapper dropped command/policy at the time of 012.\n- `P/013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md`: brief delivery answered 119 of 144; OpenCode mapper keeps `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`, `needsMode`; delivery leg in `/doctor:setup` reads DEGRADED for unapproved Codex hooks.\n- `P/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/implementation-summary.md`: typed delivery 44/44 (24 own, 20 attached); `TRACKED_COMMANDS` table; visibility `claude 32/44, cursor 44/44`; hook health only with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1`.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 6\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T06:12:04Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach-3\\ndescription: Segment three offer-reach lane: remaining plain tune rows after phase 012, intent-signal enrichment and re-embedding, and the degraded fallback path.\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"offer reach segment three strategy\\\"\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\nversion: 1.0.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - offer-reach-3\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the segment-three `offer-reach-3` fan-out lineage. Tracks what is left of the plain command-offer bottleneck after phases 011, 012 and 013, and the fallback path.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Read at every iteration befo