{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551028041,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d393950b001PpPd49uXU1CXrB","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d39381c3001MBWkch7m5lvN2N","type":"tool","id":"call_468ed3de699f4a389ceeb576","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt, lines 1-25\n1: Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\n2: Advisor: prompt skipped.\n3: Advisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n4: # Line 2 above is the task's exact prompt \"use the system-deep-loop skill\". The prompt policy skipped it:\n5: # shouldFireAdvisor returned {\"fire\":false,\"reason\":\"below_prompt_policy_threshold\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[]},\n6: # where \"use the sk-doc skill\" returns {\"fire\":true,\"reason\":\"explicit_skill_or_governance_marker\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[\"sk-doc\"]}.\n7: # The policy knows sk-* names as explicit skill markers and not system-* names. That file (prompt-policy.ts) is outside this phase.\n8: # Same check with a longer prompt, \"please use the system-deep-loop skill for this work\":\n9: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n10: # And \"use the system-deep-loop skill on this packet\" gave:\n11: Advisor: live; ambiguous: system-spec-kit 0.91/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.91/0.12 pass.\n12: \n13: # AFTER THE PROMPT POLICY FIX, 2026-11-13 (prompt-policy.ts now reads sk-, system-, cli- and mcp- skill names).\n14: # The task's three exact prompts, read through the worktree's own advisor daemon:\n15: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\n16: Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\n17: Advisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n18: # The same prompts with SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR set to a fresh folder while that daemon was running could not\n19: # start a second daemon, and the hook answered from the local fallback scorer:\n20: #   \"use the system-deep-loop skill\"  -> Advisor: stale; use system-deep-loop 0.95/0.15 pass.\n21: #   \"use the sk-doc skill\"            -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\n22: #   the doctor prompt                 -> Advisor: no skill matched.\n23: #   \"/create:readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.15 pass.\n24: #   \"write a readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use system-spec-kit 0.95/0.20 pass.   (live: use sk-doc → /create:readme (start))\n25: # So the fallback path keeps a typed command and loses the mode label, the doctor hand-off and plain offers.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt, lines 1-25\n1: Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\n2: Advisor: prompt skipped.\n3: Advisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n4: # Line 2 above is the task's exact prompt \"use the system-deep-loop skill\". The prompt policy skipped it:\n5: # shouldFireAdvisor returned {\"fire\":false,\"reason\":\"below_prompt_policy_threshold\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[]},\n6: # where \"use the sk-doc skill\" returns {\"fire\":true,\"reason\":\"explicit_skill_or_governance_marker\",\"metalinguisticMentions\":[\"sk-doc\"]}.\n7: # The policy knows sk-* names as explicit skill markers and not system-* names. That file (prompt-policy.ts) is outside this phase.\n8: # Same check with a longer prompt, \"please use the system-deep-loop skill for this work\":\n9: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n10: # And \"use the system-deep-loop skill on this packet\" gave:\n11: Advisor: live; ambiguous: system-spec-kit 0.91/0.16 vs system-deep-loop 0.91/0.12 pass.\n12: \n13: # AFTER THE PROMPT POLICY FIX, 2026-11-13 (prompt-policy.ts now reads sk-, system-, cli- and mcp- skill names).\n14: # The task's three exact prompts, read through the worktree's own advisor daemon:\n15: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\n16: Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\n17: Advisor: live; use system-skilled-doctor → /doctor:agents-md check (run) 0.80/0.26 pass.\n18: # The same prompts with SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR set to a fresh folder while that daemon was running could not\n19: # start a second daemon, and the hook answered from the local fallback scorer:\n20: #   \"use the system-deep-loop skill\"  -> Advisor: stale; use system-deep-loop 0.95/0.15 pass.\n21: #   \"use the sk-doc skill\"            -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.15 pass.\n22: #   the doctor prompt                 -> Advisor: no skill matched.\n23: #   \"/create:readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use sk-doc → /create:readme (start) 0.95/0.15 pass.\n24: #   \"write a readme for the utils folder\" -> Advisor: stale; use system-spec-kit 0.95/0.20 pass.   (live: use sk-doc → /create:readme (start))\n25: # So the fallback path keeps a typed command and loses the mode label, the doctor hand-off and plain offers."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551026955,"end":1794551028041}}}}
