{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551411960,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3997367002lWzcRqy2Ae2jb1","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d39961fc001Cs068h43EaakOW","type":"tool","id":"call_0a23646c2b9f42cbb245da9e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":140,"offset":2306,"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 2306-2445\n2306:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2307:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2308:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2309:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2310:             fi\n2311:           done\n2312:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2313:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2314: \n2315:       step_writeback_spec_findings:\n2316:         action: \"Write or replace the bounded generated findings block in spec.md before config completion\"\n2317:         edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n2318:         host_anchor: \"Use the chosen host anchor required by spec_check_protocol\"\n2319:         generated_fence_begin: \"<!-- BEGIN GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2320:         generated_fence_end: \"<!-- END GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2321:         fail_closed_conflict_check:\n2322:           if_existing_generated_fence_present:\n2323:             detect_manual_edits: \"Use generated checksum metadata or an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker inside the existing fence to detect human edits before overwrite.\"\n2324:             on_manual_edit_conflict:\n2325:               append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Manual edits detected inside existing generated findings fence.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"conflictKind\":\"generated-fence-manual-edit\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2326:               halt: true\n2327:         instructions:\n2328:           - \"Read `{state_paths.research_output}` as the canonical synthesis source.\"\n2329:           - \"Replace exactly one generated findings block under the chosen host anchor.\"\n2330:           - \"Fail closed if the host anchor is missing, duplicate markers exist, or human edits are detected inside the generated block.\"\n2331:           - \"Do not overwrite a generated block that fails checksum validation or carries an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker.\"\n2332:           - \"Emit `spec_synthesis_deferred` instead of partial output when synthesis cannot safely write back.\"\n2333:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation\",\"phase\":\"post-synthesis\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"<chosen host anchor>\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Replaced generated deep-research findings fence from research/research.md.\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2334: \n2335:       step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc:\n2336:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after deep-research writes back into spec.md\"\n2337:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n2338:         note: \"Fail closed before completion if the deep-research spec.md sync breaks the authored-spec structural contract. This targeted check uses the fast Node validation orchestrator.\"\n2339: \n2340:       step_update_config_status:\n2341:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2342:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2343:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2344: \n2345:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_terminal:\n2346:         action: \"Emit a single-loop terminal row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n2347:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2348:         terminal_events: [completed, failed, stopped]\n2349:         command: |\n2350:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n2351:           import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n2352: \n2353:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n2354:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n2355: \n2356:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n2357:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n2358:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n2359:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n2360:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{config.lineage.sessionId}');\n2361:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? '{config.lineage.generation}');\n2362:           const reason = '{reason}';\n2363:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n2364: \n2365:           function readRecords(path) {\n2366:             if (!existsSync(path)) return [];\n2367:             return readFileSync(path, 'utf8')\n2368:               .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n2369:               .map((line) => line.trim())\n2370:               .filter(Boolean)\n2371:               .map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n2372:           }\n2373: \n2374:           function elapsedSince(value) {\n2375:             const startedAtMs = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n2376:             const nowMs = Date.parse(timestamp);\n2377:             if (!Number.isFinite(startedAtMs) || !Number.isFinite(nowMs)) return 0;\n2378:             return Math.max(0, nowMs - startedAtMs);\n2379:           }\n2380: \n2381:           function terminalEvent(stopReason) {\n2382:             if (stopReason === 'manualStop' || stopReason === 'userPaused') return 'stopped';\n2383:             if (stopReason === 'error') return 'failed';\n2384:             return 'completed';\n2385:           }\n2386: \n2387:           const records = readRecords(stateLogPath);\n2388:           const iterations = records.filter((record) => record.type === 'iteration');\n2389:           const latest = iterations.at(-1) ?? {};\n2390:           const startedAt = records.find((record) => typeof record.createdAt === 'string')?.createdAt\n2391:             ?? records.find((record) => typeof record.timestamp === 'string')?.timestamp\n2392:             ?? timestamp;\n2393:           const elapsedMs = elapsedSince(startedAt);\n2394:           const score = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.newInfoRatio)) ? Number(latest.newInfoRatio) : 0;\n2395:           const event = terminalEvent(reason);\n2396:           const row = {\n2397:             event,\n2398:             label: 'single',\n2399:             terminal: true,\n2400:             reason,\n2401:             at: timestamp,\n2402:             duration_ms: elapsedMs,\n2403:             loop_type: 'research',\n2404:             sessionId,\n2405:             generation,\n2406:             gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, elapsed_ms: elapsedMs, score },\n2407:           };\n2408: \n2409:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n2410:             diffData: { event, label: row.label, reason, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, score } },\n2411:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n2412:           });\n2413:           if (appended) {\n2414:             try {\n2415:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n2416:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n2417:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n2418:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation, reason },\n2419:                 event,\n2420:                 status: event,\n2421:               });\n2422:             } catch {}\n2423:           }\n2424:           EOF\n2425:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2426:         outputs:\n2427:           - status_ledger_terminal: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event completed, failed, or stopped\"\n2428: \n2429:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2430:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2431:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2432:         command: 'git add -- \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research.lock\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-pause\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.legacy-projection-watermarks\"'\n2433:         note: \"Skill-owned contract: without this stage step, operators who do `git add research-report.md` lose the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, etc.). Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the audit trail intact. Operators retain commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` to unstage anything before commit. Failure is non-fatal: log warning and continue. The exclude pathspecs keep the live lock file, the pause and run-now sentinels, and the legacy projection watermark directory out of the index; locks-and-fencing-v1, ledgers, deltas, iterations and the state log stay staged.\"\n2434:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2435: \n2436:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2437:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2438:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2439:   phase_save:\n2440:     purpose: Preserve research context in the packet's canonical continuity documents\n2441:     steps:\n2442: \n2443:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2444:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2445:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2446]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 2306-2445\n2306:             GATEWAY_STATUS=$?\n2307:             if [ \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\" -ne 0 ]; then\n2308:               rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2309:               exit \"$GATEWAY_STATUS\"\n2310:             fi\n2311:           done\n2312:           rm -rf \"$EVENT_DIR\"\n2313:           exit \"$NODE_STATUS\"\n2314: \n2315:       step_writeback_spec_findings:\n2316:         action: \"Write or replace the bounded generated findings block in spec.md before config completion\"\n2317:         edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n2318:         host_anchor: \"Use the chosen host anchor required by spec_check_protocol\"\n2319:         generated_fence_begin: \"<!-- BEGIN GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2320:         generated_fence_end: \"<!-- END GENERATED: deep-research/spec-findings -->\"\n2321:         fail_closed_conflict_check:\n2322:           if_existing_generated_fence_present:\n2323:             detect_manual_edits: \"Use generated checksum metadata or an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker inside the existing fence to detect human edits before overwrite.\"\n2324:             on_manual_edit_conflict:\n2325:               append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Manual edits detected inside existing generated findings fence.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"conflictKind\":\"generated-fence-manual-edit\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2326:               halt: true\n2327:         instructions:\n2328:           - \"Read `{state_paths.research_output}` as the canonical synthesis source.\"\n2329:           - \"Replace exactly one generated findings block under the chosen host anchor.\"\n2330:           - \"Fail closed if the host anchor is missing, duplicate markers exist, or human edits are detected inside the generated block.\"\n2331:           - \"Do not overwrite a generated block that fails checksum validation or carries an explicit MANUAL-EDIT marker.\"\n2332:           - \"Emit `spec_synthesis_deferred` instead of partial output when synthesis cannot safely write back.\"\n2333:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation\",\"phase\":\"post-synthesis\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"<chosen host anchor>\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Replaced generated deep-research findings fence from research/research.md.\",\"generatedFence\":\"deep-research/spec-findings\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n2334: \n2335:       step_validate_post_synthesis_spec_doc:\n2336:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after deep-research writes back into spec.md\"\n2337:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n2338:         note: \"Fail closed before completion if the deep-research spec.md sync breaks the authored-spec structural contract. This targeted check uses the fast Node validation orchestrator.\"\n2339: \n2340:       step_update_config_status:\n2341:         action: \"Mark config as complete\"\n2342:         edit: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n2343:         set_field: { status: \"complete\" }\n2344: \n2345:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_terminal:\n2346:         action: \"Emit a single-loop terminal row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n2347:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n2348:         terminal_events: [completed, failed, stopped]\n2349:         command: |\n2350:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n2351:           import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n2352: \n2353:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n2354:           import observabilityEvents from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n2355: \n2356:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n2357:           const stateLogPath = '{state_paths.state_log}';\n2358:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n2359:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n2360:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{config.lineage.sessionId}');\n2361:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? '{config.lineage.generation}');\n2362:           const reason = '{reason}';\n2363:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n2364: \n2365:           function readRecords(path) {\n2366:             if (!existsSync(path)) return [];\n2367:             return readFileSync(path, 'utf8')\n2368:               .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n2369:               .map((line) => line.trim())\n2370:               .filter(Boolean)\n2371:               .map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\n2372:           }\n2373: \n2374:           function elapsedSince(value) {\n2375:             const startedAtMs = Date.parse(String(value ?? ''));\n2376:             const nowMs = Date.parse(timestamp);\n2377:             if (!Number.isFinite(startedAtMs) || !Number.isFinite(nowMs)) return 0;\n2378:             return Math.max(0, nowMs - startedAtMs);\n2379:           }\n2380: \n2381:           function terminalEvent(stopReason) {\n2382:             if (stopReason === 'manualStop' || stopReason === 'userPaused') return 'stopped';\n2383:             if (stopReason === 'error') return 'failed';\n2384:             return 'completed';\n2385:           }\n2386: \n2387:           const records = readRecords(stateLogPath);\n2388:           const iterations = records.filter((record) => record.type === 'iteration');\n2389:           const latest = iterations.at(-1) ?? {};\n2390:           const startedAt = records.find((record) => typeof record.createdAt === 'string')?.createdAt\n2391:             ?? records.find((record) => typeof record.timestamp === 'string')?.timestamp\n2392:             ?? timestamp;\n2393:           const elapsedMs = elapsedSince(startedAt);\n2394:           const score = Number.isFinite(Number(latest.newInfoRatio)) ? Number(latest.newInfoRatio) : 0;\n2395:           const event = terminalEvent(reason);\n2396:           const row = {\n2397:             event,\n2398:             label: 'single',\n2399:             terminal: true,\n2400:             reason,\n2401:             at: timestamp,\n2402:             duration_ms: elapsedMs,\n2403:             loop_type: 'research',\n2404:             sessionId,\n2405:             generation,\n2406:             gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, elapsed_ms: elapsedMs, score },\n2407:           };\n2408: \n2409:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n2410:             diffData: { event, label: row.label, reason, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: iterations.length, score } },\n2411:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n2412:           });\n2413:           if (appended) {\n2414:             try {\n2415:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n2416:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n2417:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n2418:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation, reason },\n2419:                 event,\n2420:                 status: event,\n2421:               });\n2422:             } catch {}\n2423:           }\n2424:           EOF\n2425:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n2426:         outputs:\n2427:           - status_ledger_terminal: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event completed, failed, or stopped\"\n2428: \n2429:       step_stage_artifact_dir:\n2430:         skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n2431:         action: \"Stage all skill-owned artifacts under artifact_dir for the operator's next git commit\"\n2432:         command: 'git add -- \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research.lock\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-pause\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\" \":(exclude){state_paths.packet_dir}/.legacy-projection-watermarks\"'\n2433:         note: \"Skill-owned contract: without this stage step, operators who do `git add research-report.md` lose the iteration trail (iterations/, deltas/, state.jsonl, strategy, etc.). Staging the whole artifact_dir keeps the audit trail intact. Operators retain commit authority and can `git restore --staged {path}` to unstage anything before commit. Failure is non-fatal: log warning and continue. The exclude pathspecs keep the live lock file, the pause and run-now sentinels, and the legacy projection watermark directory out of the index; locks-and-fencing-v1, ledgers, deltas, iterations and the state log stay staged.\"\n2434:         on_fail: \"Log warning. Do not block synthesis. The artifact_dir may be outside a git repo (e.g., temp test fixture) which is a valid case.\"\n2435: \n2436:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2437:   # PHASE 4: SAVE\n2438:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2439:   phase_save:\n2440:     purpose: Preserve research context in the packet's canonical continuity documents\n2441:     steps:\n2442: \n2443:       step_compose_save_payload:\n2444:         action: \"Compose the structured JSON payload consumed by generate-context.js\"\n2445:         output: \"/tmp/save-context-data-<session-id>.json\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2446]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":140,\"offset\":2306,\"path\":\".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551411559,"end":1794551411960}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794551413225,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"id":"prt_1d39979e9001J0u0Y70rVnq46g","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d39961fc001Cs068h43EaakOW","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"1cd0b8ad1be075e22074cf761748e97a54764bd7","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":2910,"output":84,"reasoning":210,"cache":{"read":204416,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794551438364,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"id":"prt_1d399dc1b001yOejTCytGzbQqa","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d39979ef001dps2zTUgcTZRa7","type":"step-start","snapshot":"1cd0b8ad1be075e22074cf761748e97a54764bd7"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551471281,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39a18af0021xiSILGcliXgnL","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d39979ef001dps2zTUgcTZRa7","type":"tool","id":"call_a92cbeaf67914b51a2323676","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 6: One measurement model, the final ranked list, and what remains unmeasured\n\n## Focus\n\nReconcile the four plain-offer numbers in play into one measurement model, map every one of the 17 no-command rows to the candidate that moves it, restate the final ranking with its verification, and name the gaps that no iteration could close from inside this lineage.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Re-read the committed capture's `attachedMetrics.plain.tune`, the real-embedding capture, and the live per-row table.\n2. Recomputed the head / Also / none partition and the exact versus subcommand split from `prompts/tune-live.jsonl`.\n3. Mapped the six causes from iteration 1 onto the six ranked candidates from iteration 4.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The four numbers describe one state under four definitions: the committed fixture capture's 23 is expected-command reach through bridge row ids under fixture vectors; the real-embedding capture's 28 is the same metric under the operator's vectors; the live brief renders 27 head commands plus 1 `Also:` line, which is 28 rows carrying a command; and candidate 1 projects 30. None of them is a regression of another. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/real-embed-capture.json]\n\n2. Of the 28 rendered commands, 22 are the exact corpus label and 6 are a documented subcommand (`/doctor:agents-md check`, `/doctor:ci report`, `/doctor:env list`, `/doctor:git hooks`, `/doctor:overlay status`, `/doctor:symlink link`). Exact-string metrics therefore understate plain reach by 6 rows at HEAD, and that is a corpus-label decision for the operator, not a routing defect. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/tune-live.jsonl]\n\n3. Every one of the 17 no-command rows maps to a candidate: 1 to the duplicate-suppression fix, 2 to the sk-doc alias fix, 2 to the silent-hub label fix, 6 to the below-threshold anchors, and 2 to the wrong-top doctor fix; the remaining 4 already print `(needs a mode)` and are an intentional ask, not a defect. [INFERENCE: based on iterations 1 and 4]\n\n4. Final ranking by expected gain in started-when-useful per unit of risk: (1) sk-doc readme and human-voice aliases, +2 rows, zero floor exposure; (2) below-threshold anchors plus one scorer row, up to +6 rows, the only candidate with real floor risk; (3) the silent-hub label for `sk-code`, +2 actionable labels; (4) in-process TypeScript scoring on the degraded path, 28 rendered commands instead of 0 on untyped rows whenever the daemon is down; (5) the duplicate-suppression fix, +1 row; (6) the doctor wrong-top pair, +2 rows, medium-high risk. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-004.md]\n\n5. Verification per candidate is already executable with committed scripts: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt` for the alias modes; `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding` (no `--write`) for the tune and false-offer lines; the advisor suite for the label and duplicate changes; a new unreachable-endpoint vitest for the degraded path; and the three named floor row ids (`mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01`, `sv-03`) for the anchor work. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:36]\n\n6. Three gaps remain, all measurement rather than routing: no persistent counter records how often the local-scorer fallback answers; OpenCode's degraded behaviour is unmeasured because its delivery is `unknown`; and the six subcommand labels need an operator decision on whether the corpus should name the subcommand. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/hook-health.json]\n\n7. The lane's three questions are answered with commands and file evidence: (a) 17 rows and six causes, each named by row id; (b) re-embedding and intent enrichment declined again, measured at 0 brief-level commands and priced at about 83 ms for all 14 skill vectors with hash-gated incremental refresh; (g) the fallback runs the Python scorer and then collapses untyped rows, measured at 644 ms and 0 observed occurrences in the recorded arms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/degraded-readme.json]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reporting a single \"plain recall\" number without its definition. The four numbers differ by metric and regime, and quoting one alone would misstate the built state.\n- Treating the 4 needs-mode rows as fixable recall. They are a deliberate ask, and forcing a command on them would repeat the eliminated \"default command for a deferring hub\" item.\n- Counting the six subcommand rows as misses in the final ranking; they are reach, and only the label granularity differs.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Closing the fallback-frequency gap from inside the lineage: it needs a persistent counter that only a build phase can add.\n- Measuring OpenCode's degraded path: no delivery marker exists for the committed arm.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"plain reach\" is used in four senses in the packet; this iteration fixes one definition per number.\n- Contradictory evidence: the 012 summary's claim that the deep rows attach their commands against the committed capture's `offered: false` is resolved by the field definition, not by a code difference.\n- Missing dependencies: none new.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/tune-live.jsonl`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/real-embed-capture.json`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/degraded-readme.json`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-001.md`, `iteration-004.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:36`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/hook-health.json`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.2\n- Questions addressed: the reconciliation of the four plain-offer numbers and the closure of the lane's three questions\n- Questions answered: none newly; the three lane questions were answered in iterations 1 to 3 and are restated here with their evidence\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: mapping each cause to a candidate forced the ranking to cover all 17 rows instead of the three most visible ones.\n- What did not work and why: earlier iterations quoted 23, 27 and 28 without a shared definition, which read as disagreement; the model now assigns one definition per number.\n- What I would do differently: define the measurement model before the first row measurement, so every later iteration quotes the same one.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nSynthesis: write the lane's final research document with the ranked recommendations, each one's file, measured gain, verification command and floor risk, the declined items with their reasons, and the convergence report.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 6: One measurement model, the final ranked list, and what remains unmeasured\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nReconcile the four plain-offer numbers in play into one measurement model, map every one of the 17 no-command rows to the candidate that moves it, restate the final ranking with its verification, and name the gaps that no iteration could close from inside this lineage.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Re-read the committed capture's `attachedMetrics.plain.tune`, the real-embedding capture, and the live per-row table.\\n2. Recomputed the head / Also / none partition and the exact versus subcommand split from `prompts/tune-live.jsonl`.\\n3. Mapped the six causes from iteration 1 onto the six ranked candidates from iteration 4.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The four numbers describe one state under four definitions: the committed fixture capture's 23 is expected-command reach through bridge row ids under fixture vectors; the real-embedding capture's 28 is the same metric under the operator's vectors; the live brief renders 27 head commands plus 1 `Also:` line, which is 28 rows carrying a command; and candidate 1 projects 30. None of them is a regression of another. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/real-embed-capture.json]\\n\\n2. Of the 28 rendered commands, 22 are the exact corpus label and 6 are a documented subcommand (`/doctor:agents-md check`, `/doctor:ci report`, `/doctor:env list`, `/doctor:git hooks`, `/doctor:overlay status`, `/doctor:symlink link`). Exact-string metrics therefore understate plain reach by 6 rows at HEAD, and that is a corpus-label decision for the operator, not a routing defect. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/tune-live.jsonl]\\n\\n3. Every one of the 17 no-command rows maps to a candidate: 1 to the duplicate-suppression fix, 2 to the sk-doc alias fix, 2 to the silent-hub label fix, 6 to the below-threshold anchors, and 2 to the wrong-top doctor fix; the remaining 4 already print `(needs a mode)` and are an intentional ask, not a defect. [INFERENCE: based on iterations 1 and 4]\\n\\n4. Final ranking by expected gain in started-when-useful per unit of risk: (1) sk-doc readme and human-voice aliases, +2 rows, zero floor exposure; (2) below-threshold anchors plus one scorer row, up to +6 rows, the only candidate with real floor risk; (3) the silent-hub label for `sk-code`, +2 actionable labels; (4) in-process TypeScript scoring on the degraded path, 28 rendered commands instead of 0 on untyped rows whenever the daemon is down; (5) the duplicate-suppression fix, +1 row; (6) the doctor wrong-top pair, +2 rows, medium-high risk. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-004.md]\\n\\n5. Verification per candidate is already executable with committed scripts: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc --prompt` for the alias modes; `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding` (no `--write`) for the tune and false-offer lines; the advisor suite for the label and duplicate changes; a new unreachable-endpoint vitest for the degraded path; and the three named floor row ids (`mns-chat-03`, `nm-system-skilled-doctor-01`, `sv-03`) for the anchor work. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:36]\\n\\n6. Three gaps remain, all measurement rather than routing: no persistent counter records how often the local-scorer fallback answers; OpenCode's degraded behaviour is unmeasured because its delivery is `unknown`; and the six subcommand labels need an operator decision on whether the corpus should name the subcommand. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/hook-health.json]\\n\\n7. The lane's three questions are answered with commands and file evidence: (a) 17 rows and six causes, each named by row id; (b) re-embedding and intent enrichment declined again, measured at 0 brief-level commands and priced at about 83 ms for all 14 skill vectors with hash-gated incremental refresh; (g) the fallback runs the Python scorer and then collapses untyped rows, measured at 644 ms and 0 observed occurrences in the recorded arms. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/degraded-readme.json]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Reporting a single \\\"plain recall\\\" number without its definition. The four numbers differ by metric and regime, and quoting one alone would misstate the built state.\\n- Treating the 4 needs-mode rows as fixable recall. They are a deliberate ask, and forcing a command on them would repeat the eliminated \\\"default command for a deferring hub\\\" item.\\n- Counting the six subcommand rows as misses in the final ranking; they are reach, and only the label granularity differs.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Closing the fallback-frequency gap from inside the lineage: it needs a persistent counter that only a build phase can add.\\n- Measuring OpenCode's degraded path: no delivery marker exists for the committed arm.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"plain reach\\\" is used in four senses in the packet; this iteration fixes one definition per number.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the 012 summary's claim that the deep rows attach their commands against the committed capture's `offered: false` is resolved by the field definition, not by a code difference.\\n- Missing dependencies: none new.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/tune-live.jsonl`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/real-embed-capture.json`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/prompts/degraded-readme.json`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-001.md`, `iteration-004.md`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:36`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/hook-health.json`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.2\\n- Questions addressed: the reconciliation of the four plain-offer numbers and the closure of the lane's three questions\\n- Questions answered: none newly; the three lane questions were answered in iterations 1 to 3 and are restated here with their evidence\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: mapping each cause to a candidate forced the ranking to cover all 17 rows instead of the three most visible ones.\\n- What did not work and why: earlier iterations quoted 23, 27 and 28 without a shared definition, which read as disagreement; the model now assigns one definition per number.\\n- What I would do differently: define the measurement model before the first row measurement, so every later iteration quotes the same one.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nSynthesis: write the lane's final research document with the ranked recommendations, each one's file, measured gain, verification command and floor risk, the declined items with their reasons, and the convergence report.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551453871,"end":1794551471281}}}}
