{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551616119,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d39c9260001fm4VrI6nSM7y2p","sessionID":"ses_e2c799d85ffebLHFzdZg0KLfFI","messageID":"msg_1d39c847c0013pZjchzkovX6iI","type":"tool","id":"call_8f3ef4e9f6bc4c09bfaad744","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Confidence: high on the 17-row inventory and the six causes (direct per-row measurement and code reads); medium on R2's expected gain (anchor wording not written); low on the fallback frequency (no counter).\n- Synthesis boundaries: the `spec.md` findings writeback, the strict spec validation and the continuity save were not run, because this detached lineage may write only inside its own folder. The parent run owns those steps after the lineage merge.","oldString":"- Confidence: high on the 17-row inventory and the six causes (direct per-row measurement and code reads); medium on R2's expected gain (anchor wording not written); low on the fallback frequency (no counter).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md\n@@ -178,8 +178,9 @@\n - The recommendations are projections except R1's canary count, which is measured. Each names the command that measures it.\n - Holdout prompt text was never read; holdout appears only as counts (1 to 3 of 44).\n - The 23-to-28 difference between the committed capture and the real capture is a regime difference at one commit, not a change in code.\n - Confidence: high on the 17-row inventory and the six causes (direct per-row measurement and code reads); medium on R2's expected gain (anchor wording not written); low on the fallback frequency (no counter).\n+- Synthesis boundaries: the `spec.md` findings writeback, the strict spec validation and the continuity save were not run, because this detached lineage may write only inside its own folder. The parent run owns those steps after the lineage merge.\n \n ## 16. Implementation Decision\n \n Build R1 first: it is two alias phrases, two rows, and zero measured floor exposure. Then R2 with the three named floor rows in its check, because it is the only candidate that can move more than two rows. R3 and R5 are cheap label and head fixes that ride along with either. R4 should follow, because it removes a silently different answer on every hook runtime whenever the daemon is down. R6 needs an explicit policy call on a default doctor subcommand before it is scheduled. Nothing here re-decides a segment-one or segment-two item.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Confidence: high on the 17-row inventory and the six causes (direct per-row measurement and code reads); medium on R2's expected gain (anchor wording not written); low on the fallback frequency (no counter).\\n- Synthesis boundaries: the `spec.md` findings writeback, the strict spec validation and the continuity save were not run, because this detached lineage may write only inside its own folder. The parent run owns those steps after the lineage merge.\",\"oldString\":\"- Confidence: high on the 17-row inventory and the six causes (direct per-row measurement and code reads); medium on R2's expected gain (anchor wording not written); low on the fallback frequency (no counter).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/offer-reach-3/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551616096,"end":1794551616119}}}}
